Subject: Critical Security Update — Action Required
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 16:30:00 +0000
From: IT Security Desk <it-security@resistance.org>
To: All Staff <all-staff@resistance.org>

ATTENTION: ALL USERS

A critical vulnerability has been discovered in the OpenSSL
library used by our email infrastructure (CVE-2026-1234).
This affects all versions prior to 3.2.5.

WHAT YOU NEED TO DO:

1. UPDATE YOUR CLIENTS
   Make sure your email client is running the latest version.
   For Puffin users: run `puffin update` or download the
   latest binary from the internal repository.

2. ROTATE YOUR CREDENTIALS
   Change your email password and any application-specific
   passwords. Use the password manager to generate strong,
   unique passwords.

3. ENABLE TWO-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION
   If you haven't already, set up 2FA for your email account.
   Contact IT if you need assistance.

4. REPORT SUSPICIOUS ACTIVITY
   If you notice any unusual emails or account activity,
   report it immediately to it-security@resistance.org.

TIMELINE:
  * Patches must be applied by Friday, June 19th.
  * Systems not patched by the deadline will be temporarily
    suspended from network access.

We apologize for the short notice. This vulnerability is being
actively exploited in the wild.

Thank you for your cooperation.

— IT Security Team
